<title>UK: Lonrho says Bock to quit as deputy chairman.</title>
<headline>Lonrho says Bock to quit as deputy chairman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British general trading and hotels conglomerate Lonrho Plc said on Wednesday that Dieter Bock would retire as non-executive director and deputy chairman at the annual general meeting on March 26.</p>
<p>Lonrho said Bock would not offer himself for re-election.</p>
<p>Earlier on Wednesday Canada's TrizecHahn Corporation said it had formed a strategic alliance with Bock to expand its European real estate presence. Bock has joined the board of TrizecHahn, Lonrho said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
